 ## Background
-The method originates from research on direct volume rendering of tree-based tetrahedral adaptive mesh refinement data, where macrocell optimizations were explored to handle sparse data [S1]. It is part of a broader family of empty-space skipping techniques aimed at improving rendering performance by avoiding unnecessary computations in transparent regions.
+The method originates from research on direct multifield volume ray casting of fiber surfaces [S1] and direct volume rendering of tree-based tetrahedral adaptive mesh refinement data [S2]. It was developed as an optimization to handle sparse data and improve rendering performance by avoiding unnecessary computations in transparent regions [S1, S2]. It is used in interactive fiber surface exploration and tree-based AMR volume rendering pipelines [S1, S2].
 
